<title>FRANCE: BoF's Trichet wants euro as solid as franc.</title>
<headline>BoF's Trichet wants euro as solid as franc.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France governor repeated on Tuesday that the future single European currency should be at least as solid as the French franc.</p>
<p>&quot;The euro must be at least as solid as the franc today,&quot; Jean-Claude Trichet said during a parliamentary conference on savings.</p>
<p>Trichet has said many times recently that the euro must mirror the franc's stability.</p>
<p>He also repeated his call for investors to put their money to work, saying low market rates made it the right time to invest.</p>
<p>&quot;We have the lowest rates in Europe and the third lowest interest rates in the world. Now is the time for households and businesses to invest to make growth more dynamic and to help create jobs,&quot; Trichet said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
